<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>The Akusekijima Conflict, 2019</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;The author Robert Heinlein is credited with the remark, "Avoid making irrevocable decisions when you are tired or hungry."&amp;nbsp; Unfortunately,&amp;nbsp;in the&amp;nbsp;Twenty-First Century, much of the world is always hungry.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;This scenario assumes that a variety of factors (crop failures&amp;nbsp;caused by global warming, collapse of fish populations due to overfishing, etc.) have resulted in Chinese fishing boats violating Japanese&amp;nbsp;fisheries on an increasing basis.&amp;nbsp; Japan has protested this behavior.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;China, in principle, agrees that international law must be respected, but in the face of human suffering and civil unrest due to widespread hunger,&amp;nbsp;more than one Chinese&amp;nbsp;officials&amp;nbsp;has turned a blind eye to the actions of&amp;nbsp;the fishermen.&amp;nbsp; In addition, Japan's increasingly aggressive rhetoric about the issue, born in part from frustration,&amp;nbsp;has created tensions between the two countries.&amp;nbsp; China has become less and less willing to tolerate even lawful actions by the Japanese when it involves their citiziens.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt"&gt;-------------------------------------------------------&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = "o" ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt"&gt;Currently, one way to model a boarding operation is to move a ship or a boat within a few hundred yards of the target vessel and remain there for a certain period of time.&amp;nbsp; You will receive a message letting you know if the boarding has been successfully completed.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt"&gt;A delta template .ini file has been included in the .zip file to assist in updating the scenario to any future versions of the database.&amp;nbsp; &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt"&gt;Scenario Author: Mark Gellis&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
